Every floor Isaac reaches has a chance to be '''cursed''', which hides or alters game elements to make the floor more difficult to complete. Each curse only lasts for the current floor. Possible curses include:

{| class="wikitable mw-collapsible"
 ! style="text-align: center; width: 20%" | Curse
 ! style="text-align: center; width: 80%" | Description
 |-
 | {{curse|blind}}
 | All [[item]] sprites are replaced with a question mark and are not revealed until they are picked up.
 |-
 | {{curse|darkness}}
 | The floor is much darker, and is only barely lit by Isaac's natural aura. [[Room]]s are occasionally filled with swarms of intangible glowing particles. Fire, explosions, and lasers all cast light as normal, as does [[red creep]].
{{Dlc|r}} The aura of light around Isaac is much larger, but the darkness outside it is much darker.
 |-
 | {{curse|lost}}
 | Removes the map from the [[HUD]], similarly to the [[Amnesia]] pill, and increases the possible total room count of the current floor by 4.
 |-
 | {{curse|maze}}
 | Entering a new room (including teleporting) will occasionally take Isaac to the wrong room, with a screen-shake and sound effect to indicate the jump. For instance, entering the room to the right may instead take Isaac to the room to the left. Occasionally, discovered rooms with identical door layouts can swap contents, without a screen-shake or sound effect.
{{dlc|r}} Curse of the Maze is now supposed to only teleport Isaac into uncleared rooms, but this is bugged (See bugs section) and no longer triggers a screen-shake.
 |-
 | {{curse|unknown}}
 | Removes Isaac's [[health]] from the [[HUD]], leaving the player unable to see how many hearts remain of any kind. All health is still tracked as normal, and Isaac still urinates on the floor by the door when he enters a room at half a heart of total HP.
{{Dlc|r}} Also removes the {{I|Holy Mantle}} icon from the HUD.
 |-
 | {{curse|labyrinth}}
 | Appears only on the first floor of a [[chapter]]. Merges the two floors of a chapter; the resulting XL floor contains two {{R|Boss Room}}s, two {{R|Treasure Room}}s, and counts as two floors.
 |-
 | {{curse|cursed}}
 | Changes normal doors into [[Curse Room|cursed doors]]. Found only in the [[Cursed!]] [[challenge]] or when playing with the {{dlc|a}} "CVRS ED" [[seed]].
 |-
 | {{curse|giant}}
 | Merges normal-sized rooms into 2x2, 1x2, 2x1, or L-shaped rooms while narrow rooms are not affected ''<small>(further confimation needed)</small>''. This curse currently isn't achievable naturally in game.
 |}

