* All curses have an equal, 1/6 chance of occurring.
** If Curse of the Labyrinth is picked on a floor it cannot spawn on, such as the second floor of any chapter, [[Greed mode]], or on any chapters post-Womb, no curses will be active for the floor.
*** This makes the chance of getting cursed on floors without Curse of the Labyrinth 1/6, or {{dlc|nr}} 5/12 or {{dlc|r}} 5/18 for [[Hard Mode]] if {{E|Isaac}} has been defeated.

== Notes ==
* {{curse|labyrinth}} can spawn the same [[boss]] in both rooms on one floor.
* If {{curse|Labyrinth}} is encountered in {{s|Basement}}, {{s|Cellar}}, or the {{s|Burning Basement}}, both {{R|Treasure Room}} doors will be unlocked.
* As Curse of the Labyrinth causes the two floors in a [[chapter]] to merge, the {{R|Devil Room}} or [[Angel Room]] (if playing as [[Bethany]] or the player is holding [[Rosary Bead]]) can be encountered in {{s|Basement}} XL, {{s|Cellar}} XL, or {{s|Burning Basement}} XL, and the chances to do so are lowered as usual if Isaac takes red heart damage.
* With the Curse of the Labyrinth, it is possible to teleport into the second {{R|Boss Room}} and completely skip the first.
* {{dlc+|r}} If Curse of the Labyrinth takes effect during [[Chapter 1]], taking the door that spawns after the second boss room will lead to {{s|Downpour}} II or {{s|Dross}} II.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r}} If Curse of the Labyrinth merges {{s|Downpour}} or {{S|Dross}}, there will be two "mirror" Boss Rooms.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r}} If Curse of the Labyrinth merges {{s|Downpour}}, {{s|Dross}}, {{s|Mines}}, or {{s|Ashpit}} into an XL floor, the special rooms leading to {{i|Knife Piece 1}} and {{i|Knife Piece 2}} and their associated gimmicks will still appear.
** Only one of the "mirror" treasure rooms in {{s|Downpour}} and {{s|Dross}} will contain the knife piece; the other will be empty.{{dlc-}}
* {{r|Red Room}}s can be created adjacent to the first {{r|Boss Room}} if {{cu|Labyrinth}} takes effect on the floor.
* {{curse|darkness}} can be made somewhat easier by increasing the gamma setting in the game's [[options]].
** {{dlc+|r}} {{p|XIX - The Sun}} can now remove Curse of Darkness for the current floor.{{dlc-}}
** {{dlc+|a}} The {{i|Night Light}} can remove Curse of Darkness for the floor it's picked up. While it does not make Isaac immune to the Curse in floors after picking it up, the light beam it emits diminishes the drawback of low visibility.{{dlc-}}
** Interactions and attacks that have a controlled crosshair have their own little highlight. Controlled characters such as {{i|Strawman}} / {{p|Soul of the Forgotten}} / {{p|Soul of Jacob and Esau}} / {{t|Found Soul}} have their own full lighting like Isaac.
* {{curse|unknown}} does not affect {{C|The Lost}}, as he lacks health to begin with.
** {{Dlc+|r}} The Lost can no longer see whether the {{I|Holy Mantle}}'s shield has been broken in the current room.{{dlc-}}

* {{curse|maze}} can be exploited  to enter all types of locked rooms without spending resources. Be warned, though, as trying to enter a {{R|Curse Room}} can teleport Isaac elsewhere, dealing damage without getting him into the desired room (unless he has some form of [[flight]]).
* When Curse of the Maze triggers, it takes into account the direction the room was exited through. For example, if Isaac leaves a room by a door on the right wall, it can only take Isaac to a room that has a door on its left wall. (This also works with teleporting.)
* Since Curse of the Maze can only swap rooms with identical door layouts, if one of the rooms has a wall where the other had a door, a secret room is guaranteed to be there.
* Curse of the Maze can interfere with teleportation cards, but {{p|Joker}} is unaffected.
* With Curse of the Maze active, using any form of extra life or revival item can put Isaac into a previously unvisited room.
* {{dlc+|nr}} Curse of the Maze can teleport Isaac to the same room he was just in.{{dlc-}}
* Items that reveal the entire map do not counteract the effect of Curse of the Lost.
* With {{curse|blind}} active, leaving and re-entering a room which had a revealed item will change the item back to a question mark.
* {{dlc|r}} If an item is affected by {{achievement|Corrupted Data|n}}, it is revealed upon first entering the room even if {{curse|blind}} is active. Leaving the room and returning will render it hidden again.
* {{plat|3DS}} Curse of the Lost can be countered, as the player can draw a map on the touch screen.
* {{curse|giant}} will not merge special rooms, including Red Rooms, and will not affect static stage layouts, like those of [[Home]] or [[Greed Mode]].
* When activating curses via the console, curses are calculated using powers of 2 and addition. To apply multiple curses, add the number of each desired curse together. For example, <code>curse 43</code> would give Isaac Curse of Darkness, Curse of Labyrinth, Curse of the Unknown, and Curse of the Maze (1+2+8+32 = 43).
** Curse of Darkness = 1.
** Curse of Labyrinth = 2.
** Curse of the Lost = 4.
** Curse of the Unknown = 8.
** Curse of the Cursed = 16.
** Curse of the Maze = 32.
** Curse of the Blind = 64.
** {{dlc|r}} Curse of the Giant = 128.

