== Trivia ==
* Of the three curses that returned from ''Wrath of the Lamb,'' (Labyrinth, the Lost, and Darkness), two of them — {{curse|lost}} and {{curse|darkness}} — have different effects from ''Rebirth'' onwards.
** The Curse of Darkness used to hide the map, but was given the floor darkening effect in Rebirth.
** The Curse of the Lost used to simply add 4 rooms to the possible total room count of a floor, and was also given the map removal effect from Curse of Darkness.
** The {{curse|labyrinth}} remained untouched.
* {{curse|giant}} originated from the ''Antibirth'' mod, but cannot be encountered in-game without using mods or the [[Debug Console]]. This was because the room-combining aspect of the curse would often lead to buggy or unfair rooms. 
** The game is thus prone to crashing when entering a new floor; luck is required to reach an ending if this curse is enabled.
** A system was to be added that determined the fairness of a large room, such as limiting the number of enemies, but this proved to be too complicated to finish in time.
* {{dlc+|r}} There is another curse being used internally in the game, called '''Curse of the Mist'''. This is active inside the {{E|Mother's Shadow}} area and is used to disable Isaac's items.{{dlc-}}

